Generated changelog for v1.9.0

--- Technical ---
### Changed

- This release will integrate the complete M9 - Frontend Redesign milestone into `main` and add the v1.9.0 release notes, so the release can be tagged from a single coherent point. ([#244](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/244))

### Added

- This release will re-introduce inline citation badges that #207 first built, now over the sanitized Markdown answer instead of plain text - the last M9 item, so v1.9.0 ships with the badge feature complete rather than deferred. ([#245](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/245))
- This release will make the most likely next step in the ticket header a button that runs it, rather than a grey caption. ([#237](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/237))
- This release will add a keyboard-first command palette that opens over any page, anchored on the power-user `Ctrl/Cmd+K` chord. ([#236](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/236))
- This release will make every status change render immediately and reconcile with the server afterwards, rather than waiting for the full server round trip. ([#235](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/235))
- This release will make the Change Status and Assign/Reassign buttons inline popovers anchored to the header actions, rather than modal dialogs. ([#234](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/234))
- This release will anchor citations to the answer text in the assistant chat, rather than rendering them as a flat 'Sources' list. ([#233](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/233))
- This release will inject the agent roster into the system prompt, so the model can name the valid agents without a failed `assign_ticket` call first. ([#221](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/221))
- This release will enforce the grounding check via `tool_choice`, so the model must verify a KB-grounded answer before the first streamed token. ([#218](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/218))
- This release will make `Theme/DesignTokens.cs` the single source for the palette, spacing and radius scales, elevation, and the semantic chip colours, replacing all hard-coded colour literals, spacing and radius values, and other style elements. ([#213](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/213))

### Fixed

- This release will wrap the title `<a>` in a `board-card__title-row` div, so the `-webkit-line-clamp` is not blockified and the title is clamped to two lines. ([#240](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/240))
- This release will target the panel through `::deep .assistant-chat`, so the send button sits within the composer panel's bounds and the input and button stay aligned at any width. ([#239](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/239))
- This release will give the `Category` column a `140px` width and render it with the same `tickets-table__label` class as its neighbours, so it no longer overlaps `Due` and reads correctly as `CATEGORY`. ([#238](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/238))
- This release will add a paragraph in the chat system prompt that establishes a write honesty policy and a no needless confirmation policy, changing what the model is allowed to assert and when it must ask for user confirmation. ([#223](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/223))
- This release will render summary timestamps in the user's timezone by converting every timestamp to the user's timezone before it reaches the model. ([#222](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/222))
- This release will make the `search_knowledge_base` tool return `IsError: true` for a failed knowledge-base search, so it is distinguishable from an 'unavailable' result and can be counted as an error in the dashboard. ([#220](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/220))
- This release will score grounding by meaning, not word overlap, so correct paraphrases and translations are recognized as grounded. ([#219](https://github.com/goldbarth/ServiceDeskLite/pull/219))
